      "writtenOn": "2017-07-25T03:47:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am wondering if this is the right way to go. EVENT_MASK_S0IX is not truly an event mask of its own. Instead it is a mask that is used in the form of wake mask. \n\nI feel it would be better if this can be maintained at the power/intel_x86 level rather than at lpc level in chip i.e. host command can be used by coreboot/kernel to indicate to EC the wake mask for S0ix. This wake mask will then be stored by power/intel_x86 and used while entering S0ix instead of the static one currently used by the EC.\n\nThe only thing that needs to be taken care of is to preserve this mask in power/intel_x86 when performing a sysjump. Thoughts?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "1c50fad6602d8feb1ed069e9399b5de42eb439f3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5c0684cf_9442a8ce",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/lpc.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 63,
