        "id": 1130416
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-07-25T14:40:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In case of S3 and S5, the wake masks are defined as a host event (EC_CMD_HOST_EVENT_SET_WAKE_MASK). I intended to use similar approach for S0IX wake malso. Since S0iX is x86 specific, I agree this can be implemented as a host command in power/intel_x86.c \n\nRegarding sysjump, a static declaration should take care of preserving the data across sysjumps, right?",
      "parentUuid": "30a38ffe_6bff024c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 26
      },
